      "text": "The \"explosion\" is occurring because you have created a **Positive Feedback Loop** in your transport graph that double-counts (and eventually exponentially compounds) the amount of insulin every time the simulation ticks.\n\nEven if your ODE produces a \"reasonable\" derivative, your `Body.metabolizeTimeStep` logic is physically adding the blood\u0027s insulin back into the pancreas\u0027s insulin bucket every frame.\n\n### The Smoking Gun\nLook at these three pieces of code in combination:\n\n**1. The \"Sense\" Edge (Blood -\u003e Pancreas)**\nIn `BodyTransportGraph`, you send insulin from the blood back to the pancreas so the ODE can \"sense\" it:\n```kotlin\nDirectionalOrganEdge(\n    pancreasNode,\n    // ...\n    QuantifiedMetabolite(MetaboliteType.INSULIN, 100f),\n    type \u003d EdgeType.READ_ONLY, // \u003c--- This is the key\n)\n```\n\n**2. The Accumulation Logic**\nIn `Body.metabolizeTimeStep`, when a node is visited for a second time (which happens in your circular graph), you do this:\n```kotlin\nelse {\n    currNodePair.second.getAll().forEach { it -\u003e\n        if (it.updateType \u003d\u003d UpdateType.OVERWRITE) {\n            currNodePair.first.organ.metabolitesMap.updateQuantities(it)\n        }\n        else currNodePair.first.organ.metabolitesMap.putOrAdd(it) // \u003c--- THIS LINE\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**3. The Edge Type Mismatch**\nIn `populateQueueFromEdges`, you define what `UpdateType` is used:\n```kotlin\nvar metaboliteUpdateType \u003d UpdateType.ACCUMULATE\nif (edge.type \u003d\u003d EdgeType.OVERWRITE) {\n    metaboliteUpdateType \u003d UpdateType.OVERWRITE\n}\n```\nBecause your Blood -\u003e Pancreas edge is `READ_ONLY` (and not `OVERWRITE`), the `metaboliteUpdateType` becomes `ACCUMULATE`.\n\n### The \"Explosion\" Walkthrough\n1.  **Tick 1, Step A:** The Pancreas ODE runs. It decides there should be **5.0 units** of insulin.\n2.  **Tick 1, Step B:** The Pancreas sends that 5.0 to the Blood.\n3.  **Tick 1, Step C:** The Blood (via the `READ_ONLY` edge) sends that 5.0 **back** to the Pancreas.\n4.  **Tick 1, Step D:** Because it\u0027s an `ACCUMULATE` type, the Pancreas takes its own 5.0 and **adds** the 5.0 coming from the blood. **Pancreas now has 10.0 units.**\n5.  **Tick 2:** The Pancreas ODE starts with $y[2] \u003d 10.0$. Even if the ODE calculates a negative derivative (trying to lower it), the transport loop will again add the blood\u0027s insulin to the pancreas\u0027s total.\n\nWithin a few frames, you are effectively doing `Insulin \u003d Insulin * 2` (or higher) every step.\n\n---\n\n### How to Fix It\n\n#### Option A: Use OVERWRITE for \"Sensing\"\nIf an organ needs to \"read\" a value from the blood to use in an ODE, that edge should usually be an `OVERWRITE` edge. This ensures the organ\u0027s internal \"knowledge\" of the metabolite matches the blood exactly, rather than adding the blood\u0027s mass to its own.\n\nIn `BodyTransportGraph`:\n```kotlin\nDirectionalOrganEdge(\n    pancreasNode,\n    QuantifiedMetabolite(MetaboliteType.GLUCOSE, 100f),\n    QuantifiedMetabolite(MetaboliteType.GLUTAMIC_ACID, 100f),\n    QuantifiedMetabolite(MetaboliteType.INSULIN, 100f),\n    type \u003d EdgeType.OVERWRITE, // Changed from READ_ONLY\n)\n```\n\n#### Option B: Change the Pancreas ODE Logic\nIn the paper\u0027s model, the Pancreas is a **secretion source**, not a storage tank. \n1. The Pancreas should \"Read\" Glucose from the Blood.\n2. The Pancreas ODE should calculate a **rate** (how much insulin to add).\n3. The Pancreas should **not** store insulin itself. It should just output a `TRANSFER` amount to the blood.\n\n#### Option C: Fix the `READ_ONLY` definition\nIf you want `READ_ONLY` to mean \"let this organ see the value but don\u0027t let it affect the mass balance,\" you should modify `Body.metabolizeTimeStep` to handle a `READ_ONLY` type that doesn\u0027t use `putOrAdd`.\n\nModify `EdgeType` and `metabolizeTimeStep`:\n```kotlin\n// In Body.kt\nelse {\n    currNodePair.second.getAll().forEach { it -\u003e\n        if (it.updateType \u003d\u003d UpdateType.OVERWRITE) {\n            currNodePair.first.organ.metabolitesMap.updateQuantities(it)\n        } else if (it.updateType \u003d\u003d UpdateType.READ_ONLY_TYPE) { \n            // Only update the value if the organ needs to \"see\" it, \n            // but don\u0027t accumulate mass\n            currNodePair.first.organ.metabolitesMap.updateQuantities(it)\n        } else {\n            currNodePair.first.organ.metabolitesMap.putOrAdd(it)\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Summary of the Problem\nThe `putOrAdd` method is performing addition ($Existing + Incoming$). Since you have a circle in your graph, you are performing addition on every loop of the graph. You must ensure that \"Sensor\" data (Blood -\u003e Pancreas) uses **assignment** ($Existing \u003d Incoming$) rather than **addition**.",
